WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.776 --> 00:00:03.956
- [Narrator] Sam Holtz was
12 years old when he won

00:00:03.956 --> 00:00:08.362
ESPN's 2015 March Madness
Bracket Challenge.

00:00:08.362 --> 00:00:12.367
- I had the best bracket
out of 11.57 million people.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.442
- [Narrator] What if we told
you this bracketology prodigy

00:00:15.442 --> 00:00:17.566
doesn't even watch college basketball?

00:00:17.566 --> 00:00:18.399
- Before the tournament,

00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:20.136
I really don't watch
any college basketball.

00:00:20.136 --> 00:00:23.719
(upbeat synthesizer music)

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.064
- [Narrator] This time last year,

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.161
young Sammy was filling out

00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:33.958
his winning NCAA tournament bracket

00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:36.247
along with millions of other Americans.

00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:38.900
Sam, what was your strategy for success?

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.301
- Well, I just filled out
who I think is gonna win.

00:00:42.301 --> 00:00:43.977
- [Narrator] Was there
a science to your picks?

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.257
- No, it’s just pick whoever you want to win.

00:00:46.257 --> 00:00:48.735
There's no science, just that simple.

00:00:48.735 --> 00:00:51.958
- [Narrator] Hmm, maybe
Sammy's mom has an idea.

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:54.250
- I think he was lucky.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.330
- [Narrator] All right,
let's take a closer look

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.825
at some of Sammy's predictions.

00:00:56.825 --> 00:00:59.408
Why pick 11-seed UCLA to
make the Sweet Sixteen?

00:00:59.408 --> 00:01:01.602
- [Sammy] Because I visited their campus

00:01:01.602 --> 00:01:03.447
and I really liked their college.

00:01:03.447 --> 00:01:04.671
- [Narrator] Or 7-seed Michigan State

00:01:04.671 --> 00:01:05.731
to make the Final Four?

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:07.870
- Tom Izzo, the coach, is Italian

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:09.652
and I'm kind of Italian, too.

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:12.245
- [Narrator] Or Wisconsin to
upset then-undefeated Kentucky?

00:01:12.245 --> 00:01:13.373
- [Sammy] It kinda gets boring to watch

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.749
the same team win and win every year,

00:01:15.749 --> 00:01:17.690
and I didn't wanna see them do that.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:18.971
- [Narrator] You must
really love basketball.

00:01:18.971 --> 00:01:20.456
- [Sammy] I'm more of a
baseball/football guy.

00:01:20.456 --> 00:01:22.959
Baseball is my main sport.

00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:24.041
- [Narrator] How is this possible?

00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:25.233
I mean, what are the chances

00:01:25.233 --> 00:01:27.979
of filling out a perfect bracket?

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:30.584
We consulted bracket expert Mike Magazine.

00:01:30.584 --> 00:01:35.245
- Somewhere in one in some
number of quintillions.

00:01:35.245 --> 00:01:37.495
- [Narrator] Thanks, Professor Magazine.

00:01:37.495 --> 00:01:39.121
Any advice for the millions of Americans

00:01:39.121 --> 00:01:41.232
you'll probably beat out again this year?

00:01:41.232 --> 00:01:45.234
- Just pick who you think is
gonna win and go with your gut.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.837
- [Narrator] Remind us why
we should listen to you?

00:01:46.837 --> 00:01:48.552
- 'Cause I won it last year.

00:01:48.552 --> 00:01:50.446
(old-school hip-hop music)

00:01:50.446 --> 00:01:51.377
- [Narrator] There you have it.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.751
Pick the schools you've visited,

00:01:52.751 --> 00:01:54.060
don't listen to the experts,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.860
and don't watch any college basketball

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.791
and you too can reach the promised land,

00:01:57.791 --> 00:01:59.624
just like Sammy Holtz.

